WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:05.490
It wasn't a runaway hit, but The Boy was still
one of the strangest mainstream horror films

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:07.200
of 2016.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.720
Whether you missed out on the first movie
or just need a primer for part two, here's

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.620
everything you need to know about Brahms:
The Boy II.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:17.960
In The Boy, an American nanny named Greta
is hired by an eccentric rich family, the

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.220
Heelshires, for a very unconventional job.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.080
They want her to care for a porcelain doll
named Brahms.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.269
Hey, a job's a job, right?

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:29.400
The family gives Greta a very specific set
of rules by which to care for the doll, including

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.329
talking to him loudly and freezing meals for
him.

00:00:32.329 --> 00:00:36.420
It also turns out that the real Brahms was
the son of the Heelshires, and he was killed

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.370
in a house fire 20 years ago on his eighth
birthday after one of his young friends was

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:42.680
found in the forest with her skull crushed.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:44.010
Suspicious, right?

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:47.540
Naturally, Greta ignores the rules, at least
at first.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.329
But then, the weird stuff starts piling up.

00:00:50.329 --> 00:00:54.239
Brahms seemingly moves on his own, and a child's
voice and sobs can be heard throughout the

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:55.239
mansion.

00:00:55.239 --> 00:00:59.320
Skip to the end, and Greta discovers that,
lo and behold, the real Brahms has been alive

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:03.719
and well, and he's now a grown man who's been
living in the walls of the house.

00:01:03.719 --> 00:01:05.770
"They're in the walls."

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:07.810
"They're in the walls!"

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:11.890
After this shocking reveal, a tussle ensues,
and Greta eventually fights him off and flees

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:12.950
the estate.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:16.990
But as we discover later, Brahms is still
alive, and he's busy fixing his shattered

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:18.240
doll.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.180
Greta might've escaped, but it seems that
the Heelshire house might still be housing

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:25.930
Brahms, and that he and his doll are out to
torment whoever occupies the mansion next.

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:29.729
In Brahms: The Boy II, a young family will
be moving into the Heelshire Mansion with

00:01:29.729 --> 00:01:31.860
no knowledge of the place's dark history.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.310
"You should Google it.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:34.310
It's horrifying."

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:37.930
When the new family shows up, the young son
of the family will find and befriend the spooky

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.409
porcelain doll.

00:01:39.409 --> 00:01:43.049
Considering that the first film showed the
Heelshires harboring plans to turn Greta into

00:01:43.049 --> 00:01:47.060
a mate for the real Brahms, this spells some
pretty terrible things for this particular

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:52.159
young boy who will be unaware of the malevolent
force he may be inviting into his life.

00:01:52.159 --> 00:01:56.290
Director William Brent Bell and screenwriter
Stacey Menear are back for The Boy sequel

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.719
to finish what they started.

00:01:57.719 --> 00:02:01.700
Speaking in an interview with Cosmopolitan,
the screenwriter discussed how the first movie

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:05.250
was built around its central twist that Brahms
was in the walls.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:08.570
Now that that's out in the open, there's no
telling where the story could go.

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:09.570
As he put it,

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:12.290
"I think there's a lot of other interesting
stuff you can focus on now.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:15.510
Because the audience knows going in what the
thing is."

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:19.620
The lead role in the first Boy movie was played
by Lauren Cohan of The Walking Dead, but as

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.110
far as we know, she's not coming back for
act 2.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:26.769
In her place, former Dawson's Creek cast member
Katie Holmes is playing Liza, a mother who

00:02:26.769 --> 00:02:29.629
moves into the mansion with her husband and
young son.

00:02:29.629 --> 00:02:33.430
As a real-life mother to a young daughter,
Holmes didn't have to dig too deeply to inhabit

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:36.459
the role of a mom terrified for the safety
of her child.

00:02:36.459 --> 00:02:39.180
In June 2019, Holmes told Entertainment Weekly,

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:43.150
"I felt like this was a story about a mother
and her child and this evil presence that's

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:47.159
influencing her child, and how that's a universal
fear for every parent."

00:02:47.159 --> 00:02:50.710
But there's also another fear that Holmes
apparently discovered during the making of

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:52.440
the film: dolls.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.910
Those things'll get you every time.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:58.330
"I tell you, this doll is pretty spooky."

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:01.760
In an interview with Access Hollywood, Holmes
stated that working on the movie was a pretty

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.129
creepy experience, especially when she was
working one-on-one with the doll.

00:03:06.129 --> 00:03:12.069
"I loved dolls growing up, so I was like,
'This is really ruining dolls for me.'"

00:03:12.069 --> 00:03:16.740
Rising star Christopher Convery, who you might
remember as depicting a young Billy from Stranger

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:20.970
Things in those season three flashbacks, is
playing Jude, the boy who becomes Brahms'

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.100
new buddy.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:25.910
Considering the history of Brahms, who had
his childhood taken away from him, it's possible

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:29.850
that Jude could be targeted as part of some
scheme for Brahms to reclaim the childhood

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:30.850
he lost.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:35.110
Or if the Heelshires are somehow still lurking
about, it’s possible that they simply want

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:38.930
the young boy to replace the son they hid
behind the walls over 20 years ago.

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:43.780
Either way, this kid and his family are probably
in for a bad time.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:48.410
Composer Bear McCreary provided an eerie classical
piano score for the first Boy movie, giving

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.230
the story a distinctly vintage, haunting feel.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:54.950
For the sequel, however, a new composer is
stepping up for the job in the form of musician

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:56.090
Brett Detar.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:00.140
The musician previously collaborated with
William Bell, the director behind Brahms,

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:05.269
by composing the nerve-grating score for his
2012 possession movie, The Devil Inside.

00:04:05.269 --> 00:04:09.760
As a solo artist, Detar's music is primarily
folk influenced, which could impact the feel

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:10.760
of his score.

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:14.510
It could also indicate that Brahms: The Boy
II could have a slightly different vibe and

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:16.180
atmosphere than the first film.

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:20.080
Originally, Brahms: The Boy II was all set
to be a summer movie, with a release date

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:22.350
set for July 2019.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:26.390
Then the film was pushed to December, and
then February, No official reason behind the

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:30.580
delays was given, but it's been speculated
the film was moved to give it space from other

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:34.130
spooky doll films like Child's Play and Annabelle
Comes Home.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:38.110
The film's original release date could have
also given the movie direct competition from

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:41.240
other horror movies such as Crawl and Ready
or Not.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:43.360
No such concerns at the start of a year.

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:47.420
Now scheduled for February 21st, the film's
new release slot will put the boy up against

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:52.110
Birds of Prey, Sonic the Hedgehog, and Vin
Diesel's Bloodshot, so if you're in a horror

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:55.980
mood that weekend, your only option is lurking
somewhere in the walls.

